# Pulumi.<stack>.yaml files are committed: they hold non-secret stack config
# (region, domains, account IDs, sizes). Pulumi encrypts any --secret values
# with the stack's secret provider, so committing is safe by design. Real
# secrets (DB password, OAuth client secrets) live in AWS Secrets Manager,
# managed outside Pulumi config. Add specific stacks below to keep them
# local-only (e.g. throwaway sandbox stacks):
# Pulumi.sandbox.yaml
